  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A periodic wave travels from medium 1 into medium 2. In medium 2, its wavelength is observed to be <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.80\"></span> times its wavelength in medium 1.</p>\n<p>Which of the following correctly identifies the ratio of the speeds <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{v_1}{v_2}\"></span> and the change in frequency of the wave as it enters medium 2?</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{v_1}{v_2}\"></span></th><th>Frequency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-label=\"A\"><td>A</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.80\"></span></td><td>increases</td></tr><tr data-label=\"B\"><td>B</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.25\"></span></td><td>decreases</td></tr><tr data-label=\"C\"><td>C</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.25\"></span></td><td>remains the same</td></tr><tr data-label=\"D\"><td>D</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.80\"></span></td><td>remains the same</td></tr></tbody></table>"
  },
